    "description": "The Allen-Bradley 22F-A2P5N113 is a single-phase input frequency controller that regulates the speed or torque of industrial motors:   \n\nFeatures: A-frame size, 240V AC voltage rating, 0.4 kW output rating, NEMA open type, IP20 enclosure, standard IGBT brake, human interface module (HIM) with fixed keypad, 10 LED status indicators, speed potentiometer, and embedded I/O ports \nProgramming and configuration: Integral LCD keypad, remote keypad, or software \nMounting: Panel or DIN rail \nAmbient temperatures: Up to 50 &deg;C with minimal spacing between drives, or up to 40 &deg;C with Zero Stacking Drives \nProtection: Drive overload protection and ramp regulation \nCommunications: Integral RS-485 (Modbus RTU) communications port \nUSB port: Allows the user to connect the control module of the drive directly to a PC \nDocumentation: Technical documentation is available in the Technical Documentation Center or the Literature Library \n\nThe 22F-A2P5N113 is part of the PowerFlex 4M compact series of drives from Rockwell Automation.",
