    "description": "Product Description\nThe Omron E3Z-T61A is a compact and high-performance through-beam photoelectric sensor designed for precise and long-distance object detection in industrial automation applications. It operates using a separate emitter and receiver, where a red LED light beam is transmitted between the two units, and detection occurs when the beam is interrupted.\nThis sensor offers a sensing range of up to 10 meters, ensuring reliable detection over long distances. It provides stable performance irrespective of object color, surface, or ambient conditions, making it ideal for demanding industrial environments. (Omron)\nEquipped with an NPN open collector output and fast response time of approximately 1 ms, it is suitable for high-speed automation systems. The device supports both Light-ON and Dark-ON operation modes, allowing flexible integration with PLCs and control systems. (Omron)\nThe sensor features a compact rectangular housing with IP67 protection, ensuring resistance to dust and water. It also includes built-in protection circuits such as reverse polarity and short-circuit protection for enhanced reliability and long service life. (Omron)\nWidely used in conveyor systems, packaging machines, material handling, and assembly lines, this sensor ensures accurate, non-contact detection and improves operational efficiency.\n�� Key Features    \n\n\nThrough-beam sensing (separate emitter &amp; receiver)\n\n\nSensing distance up to 10 meters\n\n\nRed LED light source (&asymp;660 nm)\n\n\nNPN output (open collector)\n\n\nFast response time (~1 ms)\n\n\nLight-ON / Dark-ON selectable\n\n\nIP67 protection (dust &amp; water resistant)\n\n\nCompact rectangular design\n\n\nBuilt-in protection circuits\n\n\n�� Applications    \n\n\nConveyor and material handling systems\n\n\nPackaging and labeling machines\n\n\nIndustrial automation lines\n\n\nObject counting and positioning\n\n\nWarehouse automation\n\n\n�� Short Description\nOmron E3Z-T61A is a through-beam photoelectric sensor with 10m range, NPN output, and fast response, ideal for accurate long-distance detection in industrial automation.",
