    "description": "🔍 E3FA-DP23 Description\nThe Omron E3FA-DP23 Photoelectric Sensor is a diffuse-reflective photoelectric sensor designed for accurate, non-contact object detection in industrial automation systems.\n🔹 Detailed Description\nThe E3FA-DP23 works on the diffuse reflection principle, meaning it detects objects by emitting light and receiving the reflected signal&mdash;no reflector required. It offers a long sensing distance of up to 1 meter, making it suitable for medium-range detection applications. \nIt uses a red LED light source (~624 nm) for visible and stable sensing, ensuring reliable performance even in varying lighting conditions. \n🔹 Construction &amp; Design\n\n\nShape: Cylindrical (M18 threaded body)\n\n\nHousing material: Durable ABS plastic\n\n\nLength: Approx. 45 mm\n\n\nConnection: M12 connector (plug-in type)\n\n\nProtection: IP67 / IP69K (dustproof &amp; waterproof) \n\n\nThe compact and rugged design makes it ideal for harsh industrial environments including washdown areas.\n🔹 Working Principle\n\n\nSensor emits red light\n\n\nObject reflects light back to receiver\n\n\nSensor output switches ON/OFF based on detection\n\n\n🔹 Key Technical Features\n\n\nSensing distance: Up to 1 meter\n\n\nOutput type: PNP (open collector)\n\n\nSupply voltage: 10&ndash;30 V DC\n\n\nResponse time: ~0.5 ms (fast switching)\n\n\nCurrent consumption: ~25 mA max\n\n\nOperation mode: Light-ON / Dark-ON selectable \n\n\n🔹 Functional Features\n\n\nAdjustable sensitivity (potentiometer)\n\n\nLED indicators for operation &amp; stability\n\n\nBuilt-in protections:\n\n\nReverse polarity\n\n\nShort circuit\n\n\n\n\nStable detection even in dusty or wet environments \n\n\n🔹 Applications\nUsed widely in:\n\n\nConveyor systems\n\n\nPackaging machines\n\n\nBottle detection lines\n\n\nAssembly automation\n\n\nMaterial handling systems\n\n\n🔹 Summary\nThe E3FA-DP23 is a robust, medium-range sensor (1 m) that provides:\n\n\nReliable detection\n\n\nFast response\n\n\nEasy installation (M12 connector)\n\n\nStrong environmental resistance",
