    "description": "PNOZ C1 Safety Relay is a compact and economical safety monitoring device from Pilz GmbH, designed for basic industrial safety applications. It is widely used for monitoring emergency stop (E-STOP) circuits and safety gates, ensuring immediate shutdown of machinery during unsafe conditions.\nThis relay belongs to the PNOZcompact series, known for its simple installation, compact size, and reliable performance. It supports dual-channel input monitoring with short circuit detection, providing enhanced safety and compliance with international safety standards. (Pilz)\nThe PNOZ C1 features 3 normally open (NO) safety contacts and 1 normally closed (NC) auxiliary contact, making it suitable for multiple control outputs in safety circuits. It operates on a 24V DC supply and includes both automatic and manual reset options for flexible operation. (Pilz)\n🔹 Key Features\n\n\nSuitable for E-stop and safety gate monitoring\n\n\nDual-channel safety inputs with cross-fault detection\n\n\n3 NO safety outputs + 1 NC auxiliary output\n\n\n24V DC supply voltage\n\n\nAutomatic / Manual reset function\n\n\nCompact 22.5 mm DIN rail mounting design\n\n\nLED indicators for status monitoring (Pilz)\n\n\n🔹 Applications\n\n\nIndustrial machine safety systems\n\n\nConveyor and packaging machines\n\n\nCNC and automation panels\n\n\nSafety interlocking systems\n\n\nEmergency stop circuits\n\n\n🔹 Technical Specifications\n\n\nSupply Voltage: 24V DC\n\n\nInputs: 2-channel safety input\n\n\nOutputs: 3 NO + 1 NC\n\n\nPower Consumption: ~2.5 W\n\n\nMounting: DIN rail\n\n\nWidth: 22.5 mm (compact size) (Pilz)\n\n\n🔹 Working Principle (Simple)\n\n\nSafety device (E-stop / gate switch) connected to inputs\n\n\nRelay continuously monitors both channels\n\n\nOn fault or emergency:👉 outputs open immediately\n\n\nMachine stops safely\n\n\n🔹 Summary\nPNOZ C1 is a compact, cost-effective safety relay ideal for basic safety functions, offering reliable performance, easy installation, and high safety standards in industrial automation systems.",
